Production-acceptance testing on a REAL geocoded property found a defect: when the
proximity ladder narrows to a working set with NO closed transactions (a geocoded
subject whose nearest tier holds only active listings, because sold deals are
farther away), the §12 sold-anchor cap has nothing to anchor to and asking prices
drove both the estimate and an 85% HIGH confidence. Fix: when the working set has
zero sold comps, cap confidence to medium (≤55), widen the range (auto, via the
dispersion×confidence model), and surface reason code asking_only_no_sold_anchor —
so nearby asking can never present as authoritative sold-backed evidence. No
coefficient/value change. Regression test added.

